; M4 gate: a gate shorter than a frame. At 150 BPM a frame is 4 ticks, so a
; 16th cut to 3 ticks (:gate- 21t) can key on and run out in one frame; the
; key-off then waits for the next frame's head, so every note sounds a frame.
(fm4 :tempo 150 :oct 5 :len 16 :gate- 21t c c c c e- e- e- e- :gate- 18t f f f f)
(sqr1 :oct 4 :len 16 :gate- 22t c c c c c c c c)
